  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Somatropin, a recombinant form of human growth hormone, is used to treat growth disorders such as pituitary dwarfism, Turner syndrome, and Prader-Willi syndrome. It is an approved medicine with authorised products in the European Union and is widely used for growth-related conditions.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19709937&quot;>Wikidata Q19709937</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>somatropin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>H01AC01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00052&quot;>DB00052</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19709937&quot;>Q19709937</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>22129 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
end Somatropin;
